Example 6: IF with BEGIN and END block
We can specify multiple statements as well with SQL IF statement and
BEGIN END blocks. In the following query, we want to print a message
from two print statements once a condition is satisfied.
Note: We should have an END statement with corresponding BEGIN
block.
Example 6: IF with BEGIN and END block
DECLARE @StudentMarks INT= 70;
IF @StudentMarks >= 90
BEGIN
PRINT 'Congratulations, You are in Merit list!!';
Print 'Second statement.'
END;
ELSE
BEGIN
PRINT 'Failed,Try again ';
Print 'Second ELSE statement'
END;
